The bridge troll.
You: It deserves a poem. May I?
A poem! For Grubb's bridge! Go on, go on.
Grubb is listening. Make it rhyme. Grubb likes a rhyme.
> 1. Oh bridge of stone, so fine, so wide, I'd pay to see the other side.
  2. Roses are red, the river is gray, please let me cross, I'm on my way.
  3. I am no poet. Ask me your riddle.
